  "style": {
    "name": "Lantern Temple of Saltmere",
    "rationale": "Ties minarets, towers and flank panels into one banded wall (pilasters and bands run unbroken to the body) so nothing floats; carves dark-backed recesses for the pointed portal, niches and rosette panels; breaks every wide field with slab courses, blue inlay and plinth dots; keeps orange dominant with teal, ultramarine and gold accents; holds the reference ratios (25 tall by 45 wide, 9-wide stepped dome, minaret tops level with the crown)."
